{"kind":"artifact","text":"Candidate: the ambient adjunct at cmd/gitseq-mcp on the same head, closing the sole finding of review e1dc142f. The identifier boundaries now test one shared character class at both ends. The previous form excluded every alphanumeric, colon and hash on the left but only hex on the right, so appending a non-hex word byte to a canonical identifier still yielded the canonical prefix; the adjunct could report actors focused on an event the caller never named, out of a token that merely began like one. Pinned by six added boundary cases — a lowercase non-hex letter, an uppercase one, the first letter past the hex alphabet, and colon and hash adjacency — each of which fails against the previous pattern, verified by mutating the right boundary back to hex-only and watching the test fail while the package still builds. The exact-room repair the same review confirmed is unchanged.","body":{"commit":"000317cd50141c5b8801aed58a68f39a72b27248","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}